    (uint256 oraclePrice,) = IOracleAdapter(oracleAdapter).latestPrice();
    rawCAP = Math.max(oraclePrice, cr);
}
```

If CR drops below 1.0 and `strictMode` has not yet been enabled, the oracle is always considered healthy and can feed stale or outdated prices into CAP. This can lift the refund price above what a fresh oracle would allow under stress, which is the exact situation `strictMode` is intended to protect against.

